From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: mediatek: Keep MT6789 MD power domain active across s2idle wakeup

On MediaTek MT6789, the CCCI cellular modem device (d0cf000.modem) marks
itself as a wakeup source (device_init_wakeup(..., true)) and enables
CCIF0/WDT/DPMAIF wakeup IRQs while running so incoming cellular events
can wake the AP from s2idle.

However, MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_MD omitted MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP
(GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP). As a result, genpd_finish_suspend() powered
off the MD MTCMOS rail and engaged MD bus-protect on every s2idle entry
while the modem CPU was live and registered on LTE — killing the modem
(hanging /dev/wwan0at0 AT probes after resume) and wedging the AP-MD
AXI bus across suspend cycles.

Add MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP to MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_MD so genpd leaves MD
MTCMOS on across s2idle when the modem is running (while keeping it off
when the modem is parked via runtime PM).

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h
index 24189d837..e6cf98974 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ static const struct scpsys_domain_data scpsys_domain_data_mt6789[] = {
 					MT6789_TOP_AXI_PROT_EN_VDNR_STA1),
 		},
 		.caps = MTK_SCPD_MODEM_PWRSEQ | MTK_SCPD_EXT_BUCK_ISO |
-			MTK_SCPD_KEEP_DEFAULT_OFF,
+			MTK_SCPD_KEEP_DEFAULT_OFF |
+			MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	[MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_CONN] = {
 		.name = "conn",
-- 
2.47.2
